jinjarope renders with [Jinja2](https://jinja.palletsprojects.com/) by default.
`jinjarope.engine.TemplateEngine` describes what code needs from an environment, and two
backends implement it:

| Backend | Class | Install |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Jinja2 (default) | `jinjarope.Environment` | included |
| [minijinja](https://github.com/mitsuhiko/minijinja) (Rust) | `jinjarope.MiniJinjaEnvironment` | `pip install "jinjarope[minijinja]"` |

```python
import jinjarope

env = jinjarope.create_environment("minijinja", loader=jinjarope.DictLoader({"a.md": "{{ x }}"}))
env.filters["shout"] = lambda value: f"{value}!"
env.render_string("{{ 'hi' | shout }}")  # 'hi!'
env.render_template("a.md", x=1)  # '1'
```

## The protocol

- `filters`, `tests`, `globals`: plain dicts, changes apply to the next render.
  Callables decorated with Jinja2's `pass_context` / `pass_environment` /
  `pass_eval_context` work with both backends.
- `loader`: a jinjarope / Jinja2 loader (minijinja gets an adapter).
- `render_string()`, `render_template()` (also `block_name=`), `render_condition()`,
  `render_file()`, `get_source()`, `with_globals()`, `set_undefined()`,
  `load_jinja_file()`, `add_template()`, `add_template_path()`, `template in env`.
- Errors: `render_string()` raises `TemplateSyntaxError` (a `SyntaxError`) or
  `TemplateRenderError` (a `RuntimeError`, the original error is the `__cause__`).
  Unknown templates raise a `LookupError` (`TemplateNotFoundError` with minijinja,
  `jinja2.TemplateNotFound` with Jinja2).
- `get_engine_class(name)` / `create_environment(name, **kwargs)`; `EnvConfig.engine`
  names the backend of a config.

## minijinja: differences

minijinja implements Jinja2's syntax and most of its filters, but it is not Python.
jinjarope bridges some differences; the rest are listed here.

Bridged by jinjarope:

- Jinja2 built-ins minijinja lacks or takes other arguments for come from Jinja2:
  filters `batch`, `center`, `filesizeformat`, `forceescape`, `indent`, `random`,
  `truncate`, `urlize`, `wordcount`, `wordwrap`, `xmlattr`, test `callable`, globals
  `lipsum`, `cycler`, `joiner`, `dict` (the Python type, so `x is instance(dict)` works).
- Callable globals are passed as render variables as well: minijinja turns registered
  callables into functions, which can be called but are no values (`{{ len | name }}`
  would get a string).
- Lazy filters (JinjaFiles, plugin proxies) get inspected on their first call, not
  when they are registered.
- `render_template(block_name=...)` renders the source of the block (minijinja's
  Python API can't render a single block); blocks inherited from a parent template
  can't be rendered alone.
- `{% break %}` / `{% continue %}` are built in (the `loopcontrols` extension is accepted).

Not supported (`ValueError`): `enable_async=True`, Jinja2 extensions (i18n, ...),
the `keep` undefined (`jinja2.DebugUndefined`) and custom Undefined classes,
`newline_sequence` other than `"\n"`. Undefined behaviours map to minijinja's:
`strict` -> strict, `silent` -> lenient, `lax` -> chainable.

Differences in templates:

| Jinja2 | minijinja | Workaround |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `obj._private`, `cls.__name__` | undefined: attributes starting with `_` are hidden | `obj \| getattr("__name__")` |
| `mapping.key(...)` calls `mapping["key"]` | method call: `getattr` only | give the mapping a `__getattr__` |
| `obj.name`: attribute first, then item | item first (objects with `__getitem__`), then attribute | `__getitem__` should raise `KeyError` / `IndexError` |
| methods as values (`"".removesuffix`, `map(attribute="upper")`, `attr("upper")`) | undefined | call them |
| all `str` methods | strings are minijinja strings: a subset (`upper`, `split`, `startswith`, ...), no `removesuffix` / `removeprefix` | filters (`removesuffix`, ...) |
| `"%s" % x` | not supported | `"{}".format(x)`, `format` filter |
| `{% do expr %}` | only call expressions (`{% do f() %}`) | |
| namedtuples keep their attributes | converted to sequences (`p.a` undefined) | |
| `1 / 0` raises `ZeroDivisionError` | minijinja error (`unable to calculate`) | |
| `escape`: `&#34;` | `&quot;` | |
| `pprint`: one line | indented | |
| `urlencode`: spaces as `+` | `%20` | |
| `trim_blocks` keeps the newline after `{% raw %}` | removes it | `{% raw -%}` or no newline there |
| `"\a"` and other Python escapes in string literals | `\a` stays | |
| `x is filter` / `x is test` for any value | names (strings) only | |
| `filters` / `tests` globals include Jinja2's built-ins | only jinjarope's (Python) ones | |
| `parent_template` of `render_template` | ignored (names are not relative, as in Jinja2 by default) | |

Template strings are parsed on every `render_string()` call (templates of the loader
are cached per environment).
